:PNLGRP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME=VALDTE.Validate a Date Field
:P.This command is used to validate a date field. It accepts
a date field and returns an F in the PASS field if the date
is not valid. The command is intended to be used in CL programs
to make validating dates easier and require less coding.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='VALDTE/DATE'.CL Date Variable
:P.:HP2.DATE:EHP2.
Specifies the CL variable that contains the date to be validated.
:p.This is a required parameter.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='VALDTE/PASS'.The Return Variable
:P.:HP2.PASS:EHP2. The variable name to receive the date status.
:P.The command will return an F in this variable if the date is
not valid. The variable has to be defined a *CHAR Len(1). To
promote programmer familiarity the variable name should be
PASS.
:p.This is a required parameter.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:EPNLGRP.
